## Running Unit Tests

Tests to verify compatibility with the most recent API code are in `api_collection/test/api`.
These can be ran via the `make test_collection` command in the development container.

To run tests outside of the development container, or to run against
Distronode source, set up a dedicated virtual environment:

```
mkvirtualenv my_new_venv
# may need to replace psycopg3 with psycopg3-binary in requirements/requirements.txt
pip install -r requirements/requirements.txt -r requirements/requirements_dev.txt -r requirements/requirements_git.txt
make clean-api
pip install -e <path to your Distronode>
pip install -e .
pip install -e apikit
py.test api_collection/test/api/
```

## Running Integration Tests

The integration tests require a virtualenv with `distronode >= 2.9` and `apikit`.
The collection must first be installed, which can be done using `make install_collection`.
You also need a configuration file, as described in the [Running](https://github.com/distronode/distronode/tree/devel/api/blob/devel/api_collection/README.md#running) section.

How to run the tests:

```
# distronode-test must be run from the directory in which the collection is installed
cd ~/.distronode/collections/distronode_collections/api/api/
distronode-test integration
```
